$ signet context add --help
-- stdout --
Add a new deployment context

Usage:
  signet context add <name> --url <url> [--network <network>] [--rpc-url <url>] [--source <source>] [--force] [flags]

Flags:
      --force            Replace an existing context of the same name
  -h, --help             help for add
      --network string   Stellar network (discovered from stellar.toml if omitted)
      --rpc-url string   Stellar RPC URL for sandbox commands (optional)
      --source string    Default identity for this context (optional)
      --url string       Signet deployment URL (required)

Global Flags:
      --context string         deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --insecure               allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                   write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --sign-with-key string   identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
-- stderr --
(empty)
-- exit 0 --
